==English==
[[File:Ptarmigan EB1911 vol.12 p.637.jpg|thumb]]

{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|gd|tarmachan}}, of unknown origin. The ''pt-'' comes from a mistaken belief in a Greek origin, as if related to {{m|en|ptero-||wing}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɑːmɪɡən/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ptarmigan.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
{{rfap|en|Scotland}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|ptarmigan|s}}

# Any of three [[species]] of small [[grouse]] in the [[genus]] ''[[Lagopus]]'' found in [[subarctic]] [[tundra]] areas of [[North America]] and [[Eurasia]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|species of small grouse}} {{l|en|lagopus}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}
* {{l|en|rype}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|rock ptarmigan}}, ''[[Lagopus muta]]''
* {{l|en|white-tailed ptarmigan}}, ''[[Lagopus leucura]]''
* {{l|en|willow ptarmigan}}, ''[[Lagopus lagopus]]''

